# `#[dto]`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

Marks a struct or enum as HTTP wire data. Use the facade import and apply it to application types that cross a handler's JSON/form body, decoded response, path, or query boundary.

```rust
use upwell::axum::prelude::*;

#[dto]
#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
struct CreateUser {
    name: String,
}
```

## Syntax

```rust
#[dto]
#[dto(no_serde)]
struct OrEnum { /* fields or variants */ }
```

`no_serde` is the only option. The default derives `serde::Serialize` and `serde::Deserialize`; `no_serde` suppresses those derives when the type supplies compatible serialization itself. The macro implements `upwell::axum::Dto` in both forms.

## Wire contract

`#[handlers]` asserts `Dto` only for inferred wire positions, not for dependencies injected with `Inject<T>`. Scalars, `Option<T>`, `Vec<T>`, path tuples, unit, and borrowed response references have built-in coverage where applicable. A handler can still return a server-valid opaque, borrowed, or status-only response for which the generated client cannot satisfy its decoding bounds; this affects that client method rather than making all controller routes unavailable.

On wasm targets the default expansion derives `tsify::Tsify` for typed browser bindings. With OpenAPI support enabled, DTO expansion also derives and registers schema information. Browser-only conversion does not add `tsify` or `wasm-bindgen` to a native server solely because the type is annotated.
